               <mods:identifier type="citation">Revista de Geografia (Sao Paulo), v. 3, p. 87-107.</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="uri">http://hdl.handle.net/11449/63688</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="scopus">2-s2.0-0021548888</mods:identifier>
               <mods:abstract>The division of the population into income groups is a determinant of spatial perception differentiated by people for the structuring of geographical limits. The analysis, when cartographic, can however show the distortion of reality.-translated by C.Wilson</mods:abstract>
               <mods:language>
                  <mods:languageTerm authority="rfc3066">por</mods:languageTerm>
