               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAccessioned encoding="iso8601">2018-12-11T16:41:40Z</mods:dateAccessioned>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAvailable encoding="iso8601">2018-12-11T16:41:40Z</mods:dateAvailable>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:originInfo>
                  <mods:dateIssued encoding="iso8601">2016-03-01</mods:dateIssued>
               </mods:originInfo>
               <mods:identifier type="citation">Dentistry Today, v. 35, n. 3, 2016.</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="issn">8750-2186</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="uri">http://hdl.handle.net/11449/168530</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="scopus">2-s2.0-84962450115</mods:identifier>
               <mods:abstract>In this case example, the use of direct composite resin allowed for a relatively simple, conservative treatment that provided excellent function and aesthetics, while preserving healthy dental tissue. The importance of continued follow-up and a periodic maintenance and minor repair process will ensure longevity of the restorations, the aesthetics, and the occlusion.</mods:abstract>
               <mods:language>
                  <mods:languageTerm authority="rfc3066">eng</mods:languageTerm>
               </mods:language>
               <mods:accessCondition type="useAndReproduction"/>
               <mods:titleInfo>
                  <mods:title>Direct composite restorations to mask intrinsic staining: An eighteen-year follow-up</mods:title>
               </mods:titleInfo>
               <mods:genre>Artigo</mods:genre>
            </mods:mods>
         </xmlData>
      </mdWrap>
   </dmdSec>
