   <metsHdr CREATEDATE="2026-11-10T12:23:13Z">
      <agent ROLE="CUSTODIAN" TYPE="ORGANIZATION">
         <name>Repositório Institucional Unesp</name>
      </agent>
   </metsHdr>
   <dmdSec ID="DMD_11449_159857">
      <mdWrap MDTYPE="MODS">
         <xmlData xmlns:mods="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3 http://www.loc.gov/standards/mods/v3/mods-3-1.xsd">
            <mods:mods xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3 http://www.loc.gov/standards/mods/v3/mods-3-1.xsd">
               <mods:name>
                  <mods:role>
                     <mods:roleTerm type="text">author</mods:roleTerm>
                  </mods:role>
                  <mods:namePart>Franco, Renato [UNESP]</mods:namePart>
               </mods:name>
               <mods:name>
                  <mods:role>
                     <mods:roleTerm type="text">institution</mods:roleTerm>
                  </mods:role>
                  <mods:namePart>Universidade Estadual Paulista (Unesp)</mods:namePart>
               </mods:name>
               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAccessioned encoding="iso8601">2018-11-26T15:45:30Z</mods:dateAccessioned>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAvailable encoding="iso8601">2018-11-26T15:45:30Z</mods:dateAvailable>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:originInfo>
                  <mods:dateIssued encoding="iso8601">2015-12-01</mods:dateIssued>
               </mods:originInfo>
               <mods:identifier type="citation">Constelaciones-revista De Teoria Critica. Madrid: Soc Estudios Teoria Critica, v. 7, p. 202-221, 2015.</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="issn">2172-9506</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="uri">http://hdl.handle.net/11449/159857</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="wos">WOS:000412392900012</mods:identifier>
               <mods:abstract>This essay analyzes, having as theoretical parameter aesthetic analysis of Theodor Adorno and Walter Benjamin&amp;apos;s conception of history, as the novel produced in the period of the Brazilian military dictatorship (1964-1985) was negatively affected by it. At the same time, seeks to identify and analyze the ways in which the novel responded to the state terror, through the fight by narrating the historical matter repressed prohibited, forbidden: thus highlights how he, in contrast to the official version of events, narrated socially forgotten in order to reconstruct the atrocities and massacres that occurred in the period.</mods:abstract>
               <mods:language>
                  <mods:languageTerm authority="rfc3066">por</mods:languageTerm>
               </mods:language>
               <mods:accessCondition type="useAndReproduction"/>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>literature</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>resistance</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>narration</mods:topic>
